   "finding": "The first registered run exposed a latent promotion defect inherited from the v0.5 identity salt: the fact digest was appended to the retrieval query as ordinary text, so its two extra tokens pushed one- and two-word table anchors below the frozen BM25 queryCoverage threshold (0.6) and createCandidate rejected the anchored chunk as not visible (4 of 16 target promotions: GOLD-02, GOLD-11, GOLD-14, GOLD-16).",
   "fix": "research/evidence-support/layer.js now encodes the fact digest as a punctuation identity salt that tokenize() never sees; query identity and Candidate identity still differ per fact. No Gold change, no validator change, no retrieval-policy change, no gate or threshold change.",
   "rerun": "The locked Gold benchmark and the injection control were re-executed on the amended code; amendment 1 results are the reported v0.9 numbers."
  }
